# Security Policy

Security vulnerability disclosure policy and reporting procedures for <%= it.projectName %>.

## Supported Versions

| Version | Supported |
|---------|-----------|
| [LATEST_MAJOR].x | Yes |
| [PREVIOUS_MAJOR].x | Security fixes only |
| < [PREVIOUS_MAJOR] | No |

## Reporting a Vulnerability

**DO NOT open a public issue for security vulnerabilities.**

Send a detailed report to **[SECURITY_EMAIL]** with the following information:

- Description of the vulnerability
- Steps to reproduce (including environment details)
- Potential impact assessment
- Suggested fix (if available)

### Response SLA

| Stage | Timeframe | Description |
|-------|-----------|-------------|
| Acknowledgement | 48 hours | Confirmation of receipt |
| Assessment | 7 days | Severity classification and initial analysis |
| Fix | 30 days | Patch released for critical/high severity |

After the fix is deployed, we will coordinate public disclosure with the reporter.

## Security Practices

### Dependency Auditing

- Run `<%= it.pm.run %> audit` regularly to check for known vulnerabilities
- Automated dependency updates via [DEPENDABOT_OR_RENOVATE_OR_REMOVE]
- Lock files are committed and reviewed in PRs

### Secrets Management

- All secrets stored in environment variables, never committed to source
- `.env` files are gitignored; see `./docs/environment.md` for configuration
- CI/CD secrets managed through [CI_SECRETS_PROVIDER]

### Input Validation

- All user input validated and sanitized at the boundary layer
- Parameterized queries for all database operations
- Output encoding applied context-appropriately

## Scope

### In Scope

- Application code in this repository
- Authentication and authorization flows
- Data handling and storage
- API endpoints and integrations
- Dependencies declared in the project manifest

### Out of Scope

- Third-party services not maintained by this project
- Issues in upstream dependencies (report to their maintainers)
- Social engineering attacks
- Denial of service attacks against infrastructure
- Issues already disclosed in public CVE databases

---

See also: [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/) for common vulnerability categories.
